(function () {
  'use strict';

  globalThis.DBZ_V6_STORY_DATA ||= {
    version: '6.4.0',
    sagas: {},
    characters: {},
    relationships: {},
  };

  const focusRatios = {
    5: [0, 0.3, 0.64],
    7: [0, 0.18, 0.36, 0.55, 0.74],
    9: [0, 0.13, 0.26, 0.39, 0.52, 0.65, 0.78],
  };

  const entries = (sagaId, beats) => beats.map((beat, index) => {
    const number = index + 1;
    const isResolution = number === beats.length - 1;
    const isMastery = number === beats.length;
    const phase = number === 1 ? 'entry' : isResolution ? 'resolution' : isMastery ? 'mastery' : number === beats.length - 2 ? 'preclimax' : 'development';
    const item = {
      id: `${sagaId}_story_${String(number).padStart(2, '0')}`,
      order: number,
      phase,
      title: beat[0],
      canonText: beat[1],
      characterText: beat[2],
      playerReflection: beat[3],
      characters: beat[4],
      tags: beat[5],
    };
    if (!isResolution && !isMastery) item.focusRatio = focusRatios[beats.length][index];
    return item;
  });

  const pack = (id, title, continuity, sourceNote, beats) => ({
    id,
    title,
    series: 'DBZ',
    continuity,
    sourceNote,
    entries: entries(id, beats),
  });

  Object.assign(globalThis.DBZ_V6_STORY_DATA.sagas, {
    dbz_raditz: pack('dbz_raditz', 'Raditz Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Raditz arrives, exposes Goku’s Saiyan origin, and forces Goku and Piccolo into a fatal alliance.', [
      ['A Stranger at the Reunion', 'Five peaceful years after Piccolo’s defeat, Goku brings young Gohan to Kame House to meet his oldest friends. The reunion is interrupted by Raditz, an armored warrior who has already brushed aside Piccolo. His scouter leads him to Goku, whom he calls Kakarot, and he claims a family bond that turns Goku’s simple Earthly life inside out.', 'Goku greets the impossible claim with suspicion, while Raditz treats family as ownership. Gohan’s fear shows how violently this stranger has entered a loving home.', 'A stable identity can be challenged without being erased. Decide which values prove who you are.', ['goku', 'gohan', 'raditz', 'piccolo'], ['arrival', 'family', 'identity']],
      ['The Saiyan Demand', 'Raditz explains that Goku was sent to Earth as an infant Saiyan and was expected to prepare the planet for conquest. A childhood head injury changed that course. When Goku refuses to join him or attack Earthlings, Raditz kidnaps Gohan and demands a terrible body count as proof of loyalty, leaving Goku desperate but unmoved.', 'Goku rejects bloodline as destiny. Raditz cannot understand a brother who measures strength by whom he protects rather than whom he can dominate. He refuses.', 'Origins explain part of you, not all of you. Let chosen principles answer inherited expectations.', ['goku', 'raditz', 'gohan'], ['saiyans', 'choice', 'abduction']],
      ['An Unlikely Alliance', 'Piccolo approaches Goku with a temporary proposal: neither can defeat Raditz alone, so old enemies must cooperate. Goku accepts, and they track the captured Gohan to Raditz’s landing site. Piccolo reveals a newly developed focused attack, but it requires time and a motionless target, making trust and coordination as important as raw power.', 'Piccolo is still Goku’s rival, yet he calculates honestly and offers their only viable plan. Goku trusts him because the danger is larger than their feud.', 'Cooperation does not require perfect harmony. It requires a shared goal and dependable roles together.', ['goku', 'piccolo', 'raditz', 'gohan'], ['alliance', 'strategy', 'trust']],
      ['Power from a Cry', 'Raditz overwhelms both fighters, reading their ordinary battle powers through his scouter. Inside the pod, Gohan hears his father suffering and erupts with power far beyond the adults’ readings. He smashes into Raditz and cracks the Saiyan’s armor, but the burst fades quickly, leaving a stunned child and a narrow opening.', 'Gohan’s strength answers distress rather than ambition. Raditz sees only a number; Goku sees a frightened son who should never have needed to fight at all.', 'Hidden capacity often appears under pressure. The next task is learning to summon it without crisis.', ['gohan', 'goku', 'raditz', 'piccolo'], ['latent_power', 'family', 'breakthrough']],
      ['The Hold That Costs Everything', 'After Raditz deceives Goku once with a plea for mercy, Goku catches him again and refuses to release the grip. Piccolo fires his piercing attack through both brothers. Raditz falls, but Goku is mortally wounded as well. Before dying, Raditz learns that Earth’s Dragon Balls may reverse death and warns that two stronger Saiyans heard everything.', 'Goku turns his own body into the plan’s final anchor. Piccolo lands the attack, then realizes victory has placed an even harsher deadline over Earth.', 'Commitment becomes real when it carries a cost. Spend it only in service of something worthy.', ['goku', 'piccolo', 'raditz'], ['sacrifice', 'victory', 'warning']],
      ['One Year Until the Saiyans', 'With Raditz defeated, Goku’s friends confront both grief and a looming invasion. Kami takes Goku to the Other World so he can seek training from King Kai, while Piccolo takes Gohan into the wilderness to prepare his buried power. The defenders have one year to become strong enough for enemies Raditz described as vastly superior.', 'Piccolo’s decision is severe, but it also marks the first time he invests in another person’s future. Gohan must begin growing beyond fear in time.', 'After a hard result, recovery needs direction. Name the deadline, then build toward it deliberately.', ['goku', 'gohan', 'piccolo', 'kami'], ['aftermath', 'training', 'deadline']],
      ['What the First Battle Changed', 'Raditz’s invasion reveals Goku’s Saiyan heritage, Gohan’s extraordinary potential, and the existence of threats beyond Earth. Those facts remain part of the story after the immediate battle ends. This final beat does not add another canon event; it marks the perspective earned by surviving a victory that also demanded farewell and preparation.', 'Goku’s heritage complicates his past without changing his loyalty. Piccolo’s alliance and Gohan’s courage suggest that enemies and children alike can become more than their assigned roles.', 'Carry forward the lesson: identity is practiced, courage can begin frightened, and preparation gives sacrifice meaning.', ['goku', 'gohan', 'piccolo', 'raditz'], ['mastery', 'identity', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_vegeta: pack('dbz_vegeta', 'Vegeta Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Earth trains for the Saiyan invasion, Nappa devastates its defenders, and Goku battles Vegeta.', [
      ['Two Roads to Training', 'Goku begins the long journey across Snake Way toward King Kai, hoping to learn techniques worthy of the coming Saiyans. On Earth, Piccolo leaves Gohan alone in a harsh wilderness before training him personally. Krillin, Tien, Chiaotzu, Yamcha, and Yajirobe prepare under Kami, each facing the same deadline by a different road.', 'Gohan resents Piccolo’s severity but begins discovering self-reliance. Goku treats the impossible road as a chance to arrive stronger, wiser, and better prepared for Earth.', 'Different training paths can serve one mission. Judge them by growth, safety, and readiness with care.', ['goku', 'gohan', 'piccolo', 'krillin'], ['training', 'other_world', 'preparation']],
      ['Lessons on a Tiny World', 'Goku reaches King Kai’s planet after crossing Snake Way and struggles under gravity ten times Earth’s. He catches Bubbles and earns instruction in the Kaio-ken and Spirit Bomb. The techniques offer explosive power, but both demand concentration and impose risk. Meanwhile, Earth’s Dragon Balls restore Goku so he can race home.', 'King Kai teaches through strange tests and terrible jokes, yet his lesson is exact: control must catch up with power. Goku learns quickly because he listens as eagerly as he competes.', 'Intensity without control breaks its user. Build technique sturdy enough to carry ambition over time.', ['goku', 'king_kai'], ['training', 'kaio_ken', 'spirit_bomb']],
      ['The Saiyans Land', 'Vegeta and Nappa arrive, erase a city, and seek the Dragon Balls. They cultivate Saibamen to test Earth’s defenders. Yamcha wins his exchange but lowers his guard, and a defeated Saibaman destroys itself beside him. Krillin answers with a wide attack, though Vegeta and Nappa remain almost untouched by the defenders’ best effort.', 'Yamcha’s confidence returns a heartbeat too soon. Krillin turns grief into action, but the strength gap makes every mistake brutally expensive for everyone still fighting.', 'Finish the encounter before relaxing. Confidence is useful only while attention remains awake through the finish.', ['vegeta', 'nappa', 'yamcha', 'krillin'], ['invasion', 'saibamen', 'loss']],
      ['Defiance Against Nappa', 'Chiaotzu sacrifices himself against Nappa, but the blast fails to stop the Saiyan. Tien spends his remaining strength on one final attack and dies as well. Nappa continues dismantling the group while Vegeta watches with cold interest. The defenders gain minutes and knowledge, yet their courage cannot close the enormous difference in power.', 'Tien and Chiaotzu choose one another even at the edge of defeat. Nappa mistakes their inability to injure him for proof that their resistance means nothing.', 'Effort cannot guarantee success, but it can protect time, people, and the possibility of another plan.', ['tien', 'chiaotzu', 'nappa', 'vegeta'], ['sacrifice', 'resistance', 'loss']],
      ['Piccolo Steps Between', 'Nappa targets Gohan after the child finally attacks through his fear. Piccolo moves into the blast and takes the lethal strike himself. As he dies, he acknowledges that Gohan became his first true friend. Because Piccolo and Kami remain linked, Kami dies too, and Earth’s Dragon Balls vanish with him.', 'Piccolo’s final choice completes a change that training had quietly begun. Gohan loses a teacher just as he understands the care hidden beneath that teacher’s hardness.', 'Protection can reveal feelings left unsaid. Do not always wait for crisis to make loyalty visible.', ['piccolo', 'gohan', 'nappa', 'kami'], ['sacrifice', 'friendship', 'dragon_balls']],
      ['Goku Turns the Battle', 'Goku arrives after sensing the fallen defenders and gives Krillin and Gohan senzu beans. He overwhelms Nappa with speed and controlled Kaio-ken bursts. When Nappa tries to attack the retreating survivors, Goku disables him. Vegeta then kills his injured partner for failing, clearing the field for a duel between Earth’s defender and the Saiyan prince.', 'Goku’s calm breaks when he sees the cost of arriving late, yet he channels anger into precise action. Vegeta discards Nappa where Goku protects the wounded.', 'Urgency works best when disciplined. Let grief sharpen the next decision rather than govern it.', ['goku', 'nappa', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'krillin'], ['arrival', 'kaio_ken', 'duel']],
      ['A Prince, an Ape, and a Sword', 'Vegeta survives Goku’s multiplied Kaio-ken and a redirected Spirit Bomb, then creates an artificial moon and becomes a Great Ape. Yajirobe cuts off his tail, Gohan transforms after seeing the false moon, and the battered group finally brings Vegeta down. Krillin raises Yajirobe’s sword, but Goku asks him to spare the defeated invader.', 'Vegeta’s pride keeps finding another weapon. Goku’s mercy is not forgetfulness; it is a risky belief that an enemy may yet choose differently that day.', 'Victory creates choices that battle hides. Decide what kind of winner you intend to become.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'krillin', 'yajirobe'], ['great_ape', 'spirit_bomb', 'mercy']],
      ['The Survivors Look to Namek', 'Vegeta escapes in his pod while Goku, Gohan, and Krillin face long recoveries. Piccolo’s death has removed Earth’s Dragon Balls, but Krillin remembers hearing that Piccolo came from a world called Namek. The survivors realize another set may exist there, creating a path to restore friends lost during the invasion.', 'Krillin finds possibility inside the wreckage, and Gohan chooses to help pursue it. Goku accepts that mercy and recovery may both carry consequences into an uncertain future.', 'An ending can expose the next route. Take inventory of losses, resources, and unfinished responsibilities.', ['goku', 'gohan', 'krillin', 'vegeta'], ['aftermath', 'namek', 'hope']],
      ['Strength Beyond the Scouter', 'The Saiyan invasion proves that preparation matters even when it cannot prevent every loss. This reflective beat records no new event. Earth endures because fighters with very different limits contribute training, time, courage, technique, and mercy until a seemingly invincible enemy can no longer continue.', 'Goku surpasses a prince without adopting his cruelty. Gohan, Krillin, Yajirobe, and the fallen defenders show that the decisive force was collective rather than solitary.', 'Measure strength by what it sustains. Numbers describe capacity; choices reveal character under real pressure.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'krillin'], ['mastery', 'teamwork', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_namek: pack('dbz_namek', 'Namek Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Bulma, Gohan, and Krillin reach Namek and enter a three-sided hunt for its Dragon Balls.', [
      ['A Ship Built from the Past', 'Bulma identifies the spacecraft that carried Kami to Earth and prepares it for interstellar travel. She leaves with Krillin and Gohan while Goku remains hospitalized. After a long journey through space, the trio reaches Namek and immediately senses powers far greater than expected. Their rescue mission has become a dangerous race.', 'Bulma supplies the knowledge and nerve that make the mission possible. Gohan and Krillin arrive hopeful, then quickly learn that secrecy may matter more than bravado.', 'A good plan changes when reality changes. Preserve the goal, but update the route without hesitation.', ['bulma', 'gohan', 'krillin'], ['journey', 'namek', 'dragon_balls']],
      ['Three Factions, Seven Dragon Balls', 'On Namek, Vegeta hunts the Dragon Balls for himself while Frieza’s forces seize villages and track every signal. Bulma hides near the ship as Gohan and Krillin suppress their energy to avoid scouters. They discover that neither rival faction can be allowed to complete the set, even though the Earthlings are far weaker than both.', 'Krillin favors careful movement, and Gohan strains against watching cruelty from concealment. Vegeta begins treating Frieza’s soldiers as obstacles along his carefully chosen path to independence.', 'When outmatched, information and timing become forms of strength. Choose exposure only when it changes the outcome.', ['gohan', 'krillin', 'vegeta', 'frieza', 'bulma'], ['stealth', 'rivalry', 'dragon_balls']],
      ['The Child from the Village', 'Frieza terrorizes a Namekian village for its Dragon Ball and has Dodoria attack when the elders resist. Gohan can no longer remain hidden; he strikes Dodoria and escapes with Krillin and the young survivor Dende. The intervention reveals their presence, but it also saves the person who can guide them through Namekian customs and allies.', 'Gohan’s compassion overrides the safest tactic, while Krillin instantly supports the rescue. Dende meets outsiders whose first act is protection rather than conquest on Namek.', 'Caution is not the same as passivity. Some risks are justified by the life they preserve.', ['gohan', 'krillin', 'dende', 'frieza', 'dodoria'], ['rescue', 'village', 'compassion']],
      ['Vegeta Breaks from Frieza', 'Vegeta kills Dodoria after learning that Frieza destroyed Planet Vegeta and concealed the truth. He then defeats Zarbon, but Zarbon’s transformed state reverses their first battle. Frieza orders Vegeta healed so his knowledge of a hidden Dragon Ball can be extracted, giving the Saiyan prince an opportunity to escape and steal Frieza’s collected set.', 'Vegeta’s rebellion grows from wounded pride and a buried history of control. He is resourceful, but his goal remains immortality rather than anyone else’s safety.', 'Breaking from control is only a beginning. Freedom gains meaning through what you choose afterward.', ['vegeta', 'frieza', 'zarbon'], ['betrayal', 'planet_vegeta', 'dragon_balls']],
      ['The Grand Elder’s Gift', 'Dende leads Krillin to Guru, Namek’s Grand Elder. Guru reads Krillin’s intentions and unlocks his hidden potential, then later does the same for Gohan. He also entrusts them with a Dragon Ball. The new strength helps, but Frieza’s empire and Vegeta keep closing in, forcing temporary deals that none of the hunters truly trust.', 'Guru recognizes the difference between fear and malice. Krillin and Gohan accept power as a responsibility to complete their rescue, not a license to dominate.', 'Growth is most useful when tied to purpose. Ask what new capacity now makes possible.', ['guru', 'krillin', 'gohan', 'dende'], ['potential', 'alliance', 'dragon_balls']],
      ['A Convergence of Rivals', 'Vegeta kills Zarbon after their rematch and continues maneuvering among stolen Dragon Balls. Krillin and Gohan struggle to keep their own ball and protect Dende, but Frieza realizes his elite soldiers are being eliminated. He summons the Ginyu Force, whose approaching power pushes Vegeta toward an unwilling alliance with the Earthlings.', 'Vegeta cooperates because survival and his wish now point in the same direction. Krillin understands that an ally of necessity may still turn the moment incentives change.', 'Temporary alignment is not trust. Use it clearly, define the shared threat, and keep your judgment awake.', ['vegeta', 'krillin', 'gohan', 'frieza'], ['rivals', 'ginyu_force', 'alliance']],
      ['What Namek Demands', 'The opening struggle on Namek establishes a contest shaped by stealth, scattered Dragon Balls, village losses, and unstable alliances. This mastery beat adds no event to that sequence. It reflects the earned understanding that the travelers cannot simply repeat Earth’s battles; they must read motives, protect local people, and survive opponents fighting one another.', 'Gohan and Krillin adapt without surrendering compassion. Vegeta becomes a useful counterforce to Frieza, but usefulness does not erase the danger still alive inside his ambition.', 'In unfamiliar terrain, learn before acting. Principles can stay firm while tactics adapt with deliberate care.', ['gohan', 'krillin', 'vegeta', 'dende'], ['mastery', 'adaptation', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_ginyu: pack('dbz_ginyu', 'Captain Ginyu Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: the Ginyu Force corners the Dragon Ball hunters until Goku arrives and Captain Ginyu changes bodies.', [
      ['The Ginyu Force Arrives', 'Captain Ginyu, Recoome, Burter, Jeice, and Guldo land on Namek and quickly recover the Dragon Balls for Frieza. Their theatrical confidence masks terrifying speed and specialized abilities. Vegeta, Gohan, and Krillin have little choice but to fight together while Ginyu carries the complete set to Frieza, leaving the remaining four to dispose of them.', 'Vegeta recognizes the danger immediately, but his warnings cannot create trust retroactively. Gohan and Krillin enter the battle knowing their alliance rests on immediate necessity.', 'Expertise can look ridiculous and still be lethal. Evaluate capability through firm evidence, never presentation alone.', ['captain_ginyu', 'recoome', 'burter', 'jeice', 'guldo', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'krillin'], ['ginyu_force', 'arrival', 'dragon_balls']],
      ['Guldo Stops the Moment', 'Guldo uses psychic restraint and brief time-stopping to trap Gohan and Krillin despite being physically weaker. The two Earthlings coordinate well enough to pressure him, but his unusual powers nearly decide the fight. Vegeta kills Guldo before the finishing attack, saving them while making clear that he acts for his own survival, not friendship.', 'Krillin and Gohan discover that unfamiliar technique can overturn a simple power comparison. Vegeta’s intervention is useful, ruthless, and impossible to mistake for genuine kindness.', 'When a problem ignores familiar rules, stop measuring it with familiar assumptions before acting again.', ['guldo', 'gohan', 'krillin', 'vegeta'], ['time_stop', 'teamwork', 'unusual_power']],
      ['Recoome Will Not Fall', 'Vegeta attacks Recoome with everything he has, yet the larger fighter rises from the barrage. Recoome brutally defeats Vegeta, Krillin, and Gohan in turn. Gohan continues standing despite injury until Goku’s ship finally lands. The battle has exposed the limits of their newly gained power and the price of meeting elite enemies without recovery.', 'Gohan’s refusal to quit is brave but cannot substitute for strength he does not yet possess. Recoome treats pain as entertainment, stripping combat of any purpose beyond cruelty.', 'Resilience keeps options alive, but it should not become an excuse to ignore limits or help.', ['recoome', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'krillin'], ['defeat', 'resilience', 'arrival']],
      ['Goku Changes the Scale', 'Goku gives his injured allies senzu beans after training under intense gravity during the journey. With calm movement and carefully controlled energy, he defeats Recoome and overwhelms Burter. Jeice retreats to fetch Captain Ginyu. Vegeta kills the incapacitated fighters despite Goku’s objection, underlining the moral distance that remains between temporary allies.', 'Goku’s ease comes from preparation rather than showmanship. Vegeta sees mercy as a dangerous weakness and refuses to leave enemies capable of returning on Namek.', 'Preparation can make a crisis look simple. Do not confuse visible ease with an effortless path.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'recoome', 'burter', 'jeice'], ['gravity_training', 'arrival', 'mercy']],
      ['The Captain’s Exchange', 'Captain Ginyu recognizes that Goku’s power rises when needed rather than remaining at its peak. Unable to match that potential safely, Ginyu injures his own body and uses his Body Change technique. Goku awakens inside the captain’s wounded form while Ginyu takes Goku’s body, then races with Jeice toward the others and the Dragon Balls.', 'Ginyu responds to superior discipline by stealing its result. Goku’s strength depends on harmony between mind and body, something the captain has not learned yet.', 'A borrowed tool does not bring borrowed mastery. Skill lives in practiced coordination under pressure.', ['goku', 'captain_ginyu', 'jeice'], ['body_change', 'identity', 'technique']],
      ['A Body Returned', 'Ginyu struggles to draw out Goku’s power and attempts another exchange when Vegeta gains the advantage. Goku intercepts the technique and returns to his own body. When Ginyu tries once more against Vegeta, Goku throws a Namekian frog into the beam, trapping the captain in a powerless form. Vegeta places the badly injured Goku in a healing chamber.', 'Goku survives by understanding Ginyu’s technique and acting at the exact instant. Vegeta protects his reluctant partner because defeating Frieza has become the larger calculation.', 'Recovery is part of strategy, not a retreat from it. Preserve the person needed for the next challenge.', ['goku', 'captain_ginyu', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'krillin'], ['body_change', 'recovery', 'ginyu_force']],
      ['Power Is More Than Possession', 'The Ginyu Force’s defeat clears one obstacle but leaves Frieza, the gathered Dragon Balls, and Goku’s injuries unresolved. This final entry records no additional canon occurrence. It reflects how specialized powers repeatedly changed the contest, while training, cooperation, and quick interpretation mattered more than merely possessing a stronger body or larger reading.', 'Goku remains himself even in a stolen body because his judgment survives. Gohan and Krillin endure by adapting, while Vegeta’s aid continues to carry sharp conditions.', 'Own your progress through practice. What can be taken from you is less secure than what you understand.', ['goku', 'captain_ginyu', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'krillin'], ['mastery', 'adaptation', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_frieza: pack('dbz_frieza', 'Frieza Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: the Namekian wishes revive hope, Frieza transforms, and Goku becomes a Super Saiyan.', [
      ['Wishes Under a Dying Sky', 'While Frieza confronts Guru’s guardian Nail, Dende helps Gohan and Krillin summon Porunga. Their first wishes revive Piccolo and bring him to Namek, though he arrives far from the battlefield. Vegeta discovers the ritual before a final wish can grant immortality. Guru then dies, Porunga vanishes, and Frieza reaches the group enraged by the lost opportunity.', 'Dende chooses restoration over conquest, and Piccolo accepts resurrection to defend a world tied to his origins. Vegeta watches immortality disappear even while he still values conquest.', 'A narrow window rewards clear priorities. Decide what must happen first before pressure makes the choice for you.', ['dende', 'gohan', 'krillin', 'piccolo', 'vegeta', 'frieza'], ['porunga', 'wishes', 'namek']],
      ['Piccolo and Nail Unite', 'Piccolo encounters the dying Nail, who offers a permanent fusion that will preserve his knowledge and power. Piccolo agrees after confirming that his own identity will remain dominant. The union transforms his strength and connects him more deeply to Namek. He arrives able to challenge Frieza’s second form while the others struggle simply to survive nearby.', 'Nail turns defeat into a final contribution, and Piccolo accepts partnership without surrendering selfhood. Their combined purpose is protection rather than personal glory on Namek.', 'Joining strengths works when identity, consent, and purpose are clear. Collaboration need not mean disappearance.', ['piccolo', 'nail', 'frieza'], ['fusion', 'namekian', 'transformation']],
      ['Forms Without End', 'Frieza answers Piccolo by transforming again, then assumes his sleek final form. Dende heals wounded fighters until Frieza kills him to remove that advantage. Vegeta, newly recovered and convinced he has become the legendary Super Saiyan, attacks with confidence. Frieza reveals the gulf between them and fatally breaks the prince who once served under his rule.', 'Vegeta’s certainty collapses into terror and grief as he tells Goku what Frieza did to their people. Dende’s compassion made him a target because it kept hope alive.', 'Confidence should answer evidence, not desperation. When pride falls away, truth can finally be spoken.', ['frieza', 'piccolo', 'dende', 'vegeta', 'goku'], ['transformations', 'healing', 'vegeta']],
      ['The Last Saiyan Faces Frieza', 'Goku emerges healed and hears Vegeta’s plea before burying him. He fights Frieza with speed and technique, gradually using higher Kaio-ken multipliers that King Kai fears cannot be sustained. Even those bursts fail to settle the battle. Frieza remains confident, while Goku begins gathering energy for a Spirit Bomb large enough to draw from Namek and nearby worlds.', 'Goku honors Vegeta without excusing him, recognizing the life shaped under Frieza’s control. His focus shifts from winning exchanges to creating one decisive chance quietly.', 'You can acknowledge a person’s wounds without erasing the wounds they caused. Hold both truths.', ['goku', 'frieza', 'vegeta', 'king_kai'], ['duel', 'kaio_ken', 'spirit_bomb']],
      ['Hope in Both Hands', 'Piccolo enters the fight to buy Goku time while Gohan and Krillin help where they can. Goku completes the enormous Spirit Bomb and lands it on Frieza. For a moment, the survivors believe the tyrant is gone. Frieza rises instead, wounds Piccolo, and kills Krillin in front of Goku, turning fragile relief into a breaking point.', 'Piccolo risks himself to preserve Goku’s one chance. Krillin’s death reaches the grief Goku has controlled through every earlier loss and shatters that restraint completely.', 'Support often means holding danger away while someone completes the work only they can do.', ['goku', 'frieza', 'piccolo', 'krillin', 'gohan'], ['spirit_bomb', 'sacrifice', 'loss']],
      ['The Super Saiyan Awakens', 'Goku transforms in fury, his power and appearance changing as the legendary Super Saiyan becomes real. He orders Gohan to take Piccolo to the ship and leave. Frieza, sensing the reversal, attacks Namek’s core and begins the planet’s destruction. Their battle continues across a world with only minutes remaining before collapse.', 'Goku’s anger becomes immense power, but he still protects Gohan and Piccolo before pursuing the duel. Frieza answers fear by trying to destroy the entire arena.', 'Emotion can supply energy without choosing the target. Keep one clear instruction inside the storm.', ['goku', 'frieza', 'gohan', 'piccolo'], ['super_saiyan', 'namek_destruction', 'anger']],
      ['One Final Chance Refused', 'Earth’s Dragon Balls revive those killed by Frieza and his forces, restoring Guru and Porunga long enough for Dende to wish everyone on Namek except Goku and Frieza to Earth. Goku defeats Frieza, then gives the wounded tyrant enough energy to escape. Frieza spends that mercy on another attack, and Goku answers with a final blast before seeking a ship.', 'Goku proves stronger, then tests whether victory can end without execution. Frieza cannot imagine mercy as anything but an opening to exploit once it appears.', 'Offer second chances with open eyes. Compassion does not require permitting the same harm again.', ['goku', 'frieza', 'dende', 'porunga'], ['wishes', 'mercy', 'final_battle']],
      ['Namek Is Gone', 'Namek explodes after the others have been transported to Earth, and Goku’s survival is initially unknown. The restored Namekians later use Porunga to bring back remaining victims and relocate to a new home. Goku is eventually confirmed alive but declines an immediate return, choosing to complete training on Yardrat before rejoining his family and friends.', 'Gohan carries both relief and uncertainty home. Piccolo stands among the Namekians with new connection, while Goku turns unexpected survival into another period of learning.', 'After survival, restoration takes many forms: returning people, rebuilding community, and finishing growth before going home.', ['goku', 'gohan', 'piccolo', 'dende'], ['aftermath', 'new_namek', 'yardrat']],
      ['The Legend Reconsidered', 'Frieza’s defeat ends his rule over Namek and proves that the Super Saiyan legend was not the simple guarantee of domination he feared. This mastery beat adds no new canon action. It reflects a victory built from Namekian wishes, shared resistance, sacrifice, disciplined training, and Goku’s refusal to let either heritage or rage wholly define him.', 'Goku reaches legendary power yet remains most himself when protecting others and offering a choice. Frieza possesses extraordinary strength but cannot escape the habits of fear and control.', 'Power changes the scale of a choice, not its moral direction. Character still decides where it lands.', ['goku', 'frieza', 'gohan', 'piccolo', 'vegeta'], ['mastery', 'legend', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_garlic: pack('dbz_garlic', 'Garlic Jr. Saga', 'anime_only', 'Anime-only Dragon Ball Z continuation: Garlic Jr. escapes the Dead Zone and spreads the Black Water Mist while Goku remains away.', [
      ['A Poisoned Homecoming', 'While Goku is still away after Namek, Garlic Jr. escapes the Dead Zone with power from the Makyo Star. He releases Black Water Mist across Earth, turning exposed people hostile and placing Kami and Mr. Popo under guard. Gohan, Krillin, and Piccolo become the core resistance because the crisis cannot wait for Goku to return.', 'Gohan enters a threat normally centered on his father and finds that the responsibility is already his. Garlic Jr. mistakes borrowed cosmic power for permanent supremacy.', 'Readiness sometimes means acting before the usual leader arrives. Responsibility follows the need, not the title.', ['gohan', 'krillin', 'piccolo', 'garlic_jr', 'kami', 'mr_popo'], ['anime_only', 'black_water_mist', 'invasion']],
      ['Friends Behind Enemy Eyes', 'The mist corrupts many of Gohan’s friends, and Garlic Jr.’s Spice Boys exploit the confusion. Piccolo appears infected as well, attacking Krillin and Gohan while concealing his real plan. The heroes must resist without treating controlled allies as willing enemies, since defeating the source and reversing the mist matter more than winning each painful encounter.', 'Gohan struggles to fight familiar faces without losing sight of who they are beneath the influence. Piccolo accepts mistrust to protect a larger deception alone.', 'When behavior changes under coercion, oppose the harm without erasing the person you hope to recover.', ['gohan', 'krillin', 'piccolo', 'garlic_jr'], ['anime_only', 'possession', 'deception']],
      ['The Sacred Water Runs', 'Piccolo reveals that he resisted the mist and helps free Kami and Mr. Popo. They reach the Sacred Water and spread its cleansing effect across Earth before the victims’ corruption becomes permanent. Garlic Jr. remains immortal, however, and the Makyo Star continues feeding him power, so saving the population does not end the immediate battle.', 'Kami and Popo restore millions through an old safeguard rather than greater force. Piccolo’s risky performance pays off because his allies endured long enough to understand it.', 'Solve the system sustaining a crisis, not only its visible symptoms. Relief and victory may be separate steps.', ['piccolo', 'kami', 'mr_popo', 'gohan', 'garlic_jr'], ['anime_only', 'sacred_water', 'recovery']],
      ['The Star Behind the Power', 'Garlic Jr. expands the Dead Zone and believes immortality makes defeat impossible. Gohan recognizes that the Makyo Star is amplifying the enemy and turns his attack against it. Once the star is destroyed, Garlic Jr. loses the strength to resist his own vortex and is pulled back into the Dead Zone. Earth’s people return to themselves.', 'Gohan wins by identifying the condition behind Garlic Jr.’s advantage rather than trying to outlast immortality. Piccolo sees his student carry the decisive choice alone.', 'An unbeatable opponent may depend on a beatable system. Find the source of the advantage.', ['gohan', 'garlic_jr', 'piccolo', 'krillin'], ['anime_only', 'makyo_star', 'dead_zone']],
      ['Courage Without Goku', 'This anime-only conflict closes with Earth restored and Garlic Jr. sealed away again. The final entry adds no further event and makes no claim about the manga continuity. It reflects Gohan’s first sustained defense of the planet without Goku present, supported by allies who rely on insight, endurance, and trust under corruption.', 'Gohan proves that fear and independence can coexist during growth. Piccolo’s hidden loyalty and Krillin’s persistence give him the space to make the final strike.', 'Independence is not isolation. Step forward when needed, and recognize the people who make that step possible.', ['gohan', 'piccolo', 'krillin', 'garlic_jr'], ['mastery', 'anime_only', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_trunks: pack('dbz_trunks', 'Trunks Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: a warrior from the future defeats Frieza, warns of the androids, and changes the heroes’ preparation.', [
      ['Frieza Comes to Earth', 'Frieza survives Namek through mechanical reconstruction and arrives on Earth with King Cold, expecting revenge before Goku can return. The defenders gather but know they cannot match him. A young swordsman appears instead, transforms into a Super Saiyan, and destroys Frieza with startling speed before turning his attention to King Cold.', 'The stranger acts with calm certainty where the assembled heroes feel trapped. Frieza returns stronger in machinery but unchanged in judgment, once again underestimating a quiet opponent.', 'Past survival does not guarantee future adaptation. A repaired method can still carry the same flaw each time.', ['future_trunks', 'frieza', 'king_cold', 'gohan', 'vegeta'], ['arrival', 'super_saiyan', 'future']],
      ['The Second Super Saiyan', 'King Cold tries to claim that Trunks’s sword explains Frieza’s defeat, then fails with the weapon himself. Trunks destroys him and the remaining soldiers, but asks the Earth fighters to wait rather than explain his identity publicly. At the predicted moment, Goku lands in a Ginyu Force pod after escaping Namek and training on Yardrat.', 'Trunks has power enough to command the scene, yet he is careful about what he reveals. Goku returns curious rather than threatened by another Super Saiyan.', 'Capability earns attention; restraint earns trust. Share sensitive knowledge with purpose and timing when needed.', ['future_trunks', 'king_cold', 'goku'], ['super_saiyan', 'yardrat', 'secrecy']],
      ['A Warning from Tomorrow', 'In private, Trunks tells Goku that he is Bulma and Vegeta’s son from a ruined future. Two androids will appear in three years, kill the defenders, and devastate society. Goku would die earlier from a heart virus, so Trunks gives him medicine made in the future. He asks that his parentage remain secret.', 'Trunks carries admiration for Goku alongside the burden of a timeline where help came too late. Goku accepts the warning without demanding proof that cannot yet exist.', 'A credible warning is a gift of preparation, not a guarantee. Use the time it creates.', ['future_trunks', 'goku', 'bulma', 'vegeta'], ['time_travel', 'warning', 'heart_virus']],
      ['Three Years of Purpose', 'Trunks returns to his own time after identifying the androids’ arrival point and date. Goku shares the warning while protecting Trunks’s secret, and the fighters choose intense training over using the Dragon Balls to locate Dr. Gero in advance. Families grow and alliances shift as the countdown turns a future catastrophe into a present responsibility.', 'Vegeta trains toward Super Saiyan power without knowing the visitor was his son. Goku treats foreknowledge as motivation, while Piccolo remains alert to its uncertainties.', 'A deadline can focus effort, but a forecast is never a complete map. Prepare to revise.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'piccolo', 'future_trunks'], ['training', 'deadline', 'androids']],
      ['Hope Sent Backward', 'Trunks’s intervention removes Frieza and supplies the medicine and warning needed for a different future, but it does not erase the danger. This mastery entry introduces no additional event. It reflects the story’s central exchange: one survivor carries knowledge backward, and people who have not seen his losses must decide whether to act on that trust.', 'Trunks turns grief into a practical chance for others. Goku honors that chance by taking the warning seriously while preserving the young man’s vulnerable secret.', 'Experience becomes hope when translated into useful action. Give others enough truth to prepare well.', ['future_trunks', 'goku', 'bulma', 'vegeta'], ['mastery', 'time_travel', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_androids: pack('dbz_androids', 'Androids Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Dr. Gero attacks with Android 19, awakens Androids 17 and 18, and leaves the heroes outmatched.', [
      ['The Forecast Arrives Wrong', 'Three years later, the fighters gather at the predicted location and search for enemies whose artificial energy cannot be sensed. Androids 19 and 20 attack a city, but their appearance does not match Trunks’s description. Yamcha is nearly killed when Android 20 drains his energy, revealing both the enemy’s absorption ability and the warning’s dangerous gaps.', 'Piccolo quickly changes tactics after recognizing the androids’ palms as weapons. The group prepared faithfully, yet Trunks’s future has already diverged sharply from their present.', 'Preparation reduces surprise; it never abolishes it. Update the plan promptly when the evidence disagrees.', ['android_19', 'dr_gero', 'yamcha', 'piccolo', 'goku'], ['androids', 'energy_absorption', 'timeline']],
      ['The Illness Comes Late', 'Goku fights Android 19 as a Super Saiyan but suddenly weakens when the predicted heart virus takes hold later than expected. The android drains his energy until Vegeta arrives and forces the fight aside. Yamcha takes Goku home for the medicine, while the others face a mechanical enemy designed from years of stolen combat data.', 'Goku’s preparation fails on timing, not effort. Vegeta enters with satisfaction, but even his triumph depends on others removing Goku safely from the field alive.', 'A contingency is useful only if someone can activate it when you cannot. Plan for handoffs.', ['goku', 'android_19', 'vegeta', 'yamcha'], ['heart_virus', 'super_saiyan', 'handoff']],
      ['Vegeta’s Golden Answer', 'Vegeta reveals that he has also become a Super Saiyan and destroys Android 19 after preventing further energy absorption. Android 20, exposed as Dr. Gero, escapes into the rocky terrain and steals energy through surprise attacks. Piccolo defeats him in a direct exchange, but Gero flees toward his hidden laboratory before the fighters can finish the pursuit.', 'Vegeta has reached the transformation through relentless pride and frustration. Piccolo shows that reading the absorption mechanic matters as much as achieving a new power level.', 'A breakthrough solves one problem, not every problem. Keep studying the system after the celebration.', ['vegeta', 'android_19', 'dr_gero', 'piccolo'], ['super_saiyan', 'dr_gero', 'pursuit']],
      ['Seventeen and Eighteen Wake', 'Future Trunks returns and is alarmed that Androids 19 and 20 are not the killers he knew. At the laboratory, Dr. Gero activates Androids 17 and 18 despite fearing their independence. They refuse his control, destroy him, and awaken Android 16. Rather than immediately pursue mass destruction, the three decide to find Goku as a personal challenge.', 'Trunks learns that changing history has created unfamiliar dangers rather than simply correcting his own past. Seventeen and Eighteen reject a creator who treated them as property.', 'Removing control does not settle what freedom is for. The next careful choices define liberation.', ['future_trunks', 'android_17', 'android_18', 'android_16', 'dr_gero'], ['awakening', 'rebellion', 'timeline']],
      ['The Super Saiyans Fall', 'Androids 16, 17, and 18 leave the laboratory on an unhurried search for Goku. Vegeta challenges Eighteen alone and loses, suffering a broken arm. Trunks intervenes, and Seventeen stops the other fighters from joining without consequence. The androids incapacitate the group but leave them alive, then continue their journey while Krillin uses senzu beans on his battered friends.', 'Vegeta’s new power cannot protect him from overconfidence. Krillin sees enough humanity in the androids to complicate fear, even while their strength remains an immediate threat.', 'A defeat is also information. Recover first, then separate wounded pride from the useful evidence now available.', ['android_16', 'android_18', 'android_17', 'vegeta', 'future_trunks', 'krillin'], ['defeat', 'androids', 'recovery']],
      ['A New Training Threshold', 'With Goku recovering and the androids still searching, the heroes accept that ordinary training will not close the gap. Piccolo seeks a reunion with Kami, while Vegeta and Trunks consider the Hyperbolic Time Chamber, where a year of training can pass during one outside day. This resolution establishes their response before the hidden threat of Cell is understood.', 'Trunks wants cooperation from a father who treats him as a rival. Piccolo considers surrendering his separate identity because Earth may need the power of the Nameless Namekian restored.', 'When the old ceiling becomes visible, growth may demand time, humility, or a deeper kind of integration.', ['piccolo', 'vegeta', 'future_trunks', 'goku'], ['resolution', 'training', 'time_chamber']],
      ['Forecasts, Pride, and Free Will', 'The android crisis overturns the expectation that knowing the future means controlling it. This final entry adds no new canon event. It reflects a changed timeline populated by unexpected machines, delayed illness, altered behavior, and fighters whose strongest transformation still cannot compensate for incomplete information or prideful decisions.', 'Trunks provides indispensable knowledge without possessing every answer. Vegeta demonstrates astonishing progress and an equally consequential blind spot, while the androids immediately exceed the roles assigned by their creator.', 'Use forecasts as instruments, not scripts. Stay ready to learn from the future you actually reach.', ['future_trunks', 'vegeta', 'android_17', 'android_18', 'piccolo'], ['mastery', 'timeline', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_cell_imperfect: pack('dbz_cell_imperfect', 'Imperfect Cell Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Cell emerges from another future, drains cities, and absorbs Android 17 to become semi-perfect.', [
      ['The Second Time Machine', 'Bulma discovers another time machine identical to Trunks’s but older and overgrown. Nearby, the group finds a strange discarded shell. Soon entire towns fall silent, their inhabitants reduced to clothing. Kami recognizes a threat beyond the androids and agrees to reunite with Piccolo, restoring the powerful Namekian being they once formed while Piccolo retains the leading identity.', 'Trunks confronts proof that his machine is no longer unique. Piccolo accepts a permanent change because divided strength has become a luxury Earth cannot afford.', 'New evidence can transform the question itself. Investigate the anomaly before forcing it into the old threat model.', ['bulma', 'future_trunks', 'piccolo', 'kami', 'cell'], ['time_machine', 'fusion', 'mystery']],
      ['The Creature in Ginger Town', 'The reunited Piccolo enters Ginger Town and finds Cell draining a survivor through his tail. Piccolo fights the creature and deliberately allows his arm to be damaged so Cell will explain himself. Cell claims he was created from the cells of powerful fighters and traveled from a future where he killed Trunks and stole the time machine.', 'Piccolo uses apparent vulnerability to gather information, then regenerates once he has what he needs. Cell speaks proudly because he believes knowledge cannot help an inferior opponent.', 'Information may be worth a controlled cost. Define the limit before using vulnerability as bait.', ['piccolo', 'cell', 'future_trunks'], ['ginger_town', 'bio_android', 'time_travel']],
      ['A Design for Perfection', 'Cell explains that Dr. Gero’s computer continued the work of collecting genetic material after Gero abandoned the project. To reach his perfect form, Cell must absorb Androids 17 and 18. He escapes Piccolo with a blinding Solar Flare and begins draining more cities to build power, turning the android hunt into a race against a predator designed around them.', 'Cell combines techniques inherited from many fighters but treats every life as fuel. Piccolo now understands that protecting the androids may be necessary to protect everyone else.', 'An enemy’s target can become your responsibility without becoming your ally. Protect the boundary that contains the larger danger.', ['cell', 'piccolo', 'android_17', 'android_18'], ['absorption', 'dr_gero', 'pursuit']],
      ['Sixteen Stands with Seventeen', 'Cell finally reaches Androids 16, 17, and 18 at the islands. Piccolo confronts Android 17 in a closely matched battle, but Cell’s arrival changes the stakes. Android 16 reveals hidden power and damages Cell badly, explaining that the creature’s absorption goal threatens them all. Seventeen nevertheless underestimates how quickly Cell can exploit an opening.', 'Sixteen’s gentle manner does not prevent decisive defense. Seventeen’s confidence in endless energy blinds him to a technique that needs only one successful contact to win.', 'Endurance is not immunity. Understand the opponent’s winning condition, especially when it ignores attrition completely.', ['android_16', 'android_17', 'android_18', 'piccolo', 'cell'], ['islands', 'android_16', 'battle']],
      ['The First Absorption', 'Cell surprises Android 17 and pulls him into his tail, transforming into a larger semi-perfect form. The increase overwhelms Android 16 and leaves 18 as the final requirement for perfection. Tien arrives and repeatedly uses the Tri-Beam to pin Cell down, spending his own life energy to give 18 and 16 time to escape.', 'Seventeen’s single lapse changes the entire battle. Tien cannot defeat Cell, but he converts discipline and personal cost into precious distance for the two escaping fugitives.', 'Success can mean delaying what you cannot defeat. Time is a concrete resource when others can use it.', ['cell', 'android_17', 'android_18', 'android_16', 'tien'], ['absorption', 'semi_perfect', 'tri_beam']],
      ['The Threat Changes Shape', 'Android 17 has been absorbed, Cell has advanced to a semi-perfect state, and Android 18 remains hidden with the damaged Android 16. Goku rescues Tien and Piccolo from the battlefield, while the chamber-trained Saiyans prepare to emerge. This resolution closes Cell’s imperfect phase without advancing into the choices that will enable his final transformation.', 'Tien proves that an outmatched defender can still reshape the timeline of a battle. Cell gains power, yet his dependence on Eighteen remains a clear and exploitable limit.', 'After containment fails, redraw the boundary quickly. Identify what the threat still needs and deny it.', ['cell', 'android_18', 'android_16', 'tien', 'goku'], ['resolution', 'semi_perfect', 'containment']],
      ['Understanding the Predator', 'Cell’s imperfect campaign reveals a threat assembled from familiar fighters but governed by a new purpose: consume people, absorb two androids, and evolve. This mastery beat adds no later event. It reflects the value of Piccolo’s investigation, Bulma’s evidence, Sixteen’s resistance, and Tien’s delay in making an otherwise hidden design understandable.', 'Cell inherits techniques without inheriting the relationships that gave them meaning. The defenders repeatedly gain ground by sharing knowledge and protecting people he reduces to ingredients.', 'Knowing how a threat grows is part of defeating it. Study dependencies, not only present strength.', ['cell', 'piccolo', 'android_16', 'tien', 'bulma'], ['mastery', 'investigation', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_cell_perfect: pack('dbz_cell_perfect', 'Perfect Cell Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Vegeta and Trunks challenge semi-perfect Cell, Cell absorbs Android 18, and the Cell Games are announced.', [
      ['A Year Behind One Door', 'Vegeta and Trunks leave the Hyperbolic Time Chamber with power far beyond their earlier Super Saiyan forms. Vegeta, calling himself Super Vegeta, intercepts semi-perfect Cell and dominates him. Trunks has also grown enormously but holds back to avoid eclipsing his father. Their training has produced the strength needed to end the crisis and new reasons not to use it cleanly.', 'Vegeta treats the gap over Cell as proof of personal supremacy. Trunks balances urgency against a painful desire to preserve his father’s dignity in practice.', 'Growth can create emotional risks alongside capability. Do not let status obstruct the result the training was meant to secure.', ['vegeta', 'future_trunks', 'cell'], ['time_chamber', 'super_vegeta', 'pride']],
      ['Cell Becomes Perfect', 'Cell persuades Vegeta to permit the search for Android 18, appealing to his desire for a stronger challenge. Trunks objects and clashes with his father, while Krillin cannot use Bulma’s shutdown controller on Eighteen. Cell exploits those separate choices, reaches Eighteen with a Solar Flare, and absorbs her. His completed form immediately reveals power beyond Vegeta, shifting the objective from prevention to survival.', 'Vegeta risks the planet for pride, while Krillin spares a person rather than a device. Cell turns both motives into openings, and Eighteen loses her freedom.', 'A preventable escalation demands honesty, not blame alone. Face the new condition while preserving its causes as lessons.', ['cell', 'android_18', 'vegeta', 'future_trunks', 'krillin'], ['perfect_cell', 'absorption', 'choice']],
      ['The Weight of Greater Power', 'Trunks expands his muscles into an advanced Super Saiyan state and briefly appears strong enough to challenge Perfect Cell. Cell exposes the form’s fatal weakness: its bulk sacrifices the speed needed to land a decisive blow. Trunks realizes that Vegeta likely understood the same limitation and abandons the contest rather than mistake impressive force for usable superiority.', 'Trunks can admit his solution failed once the evidence is undeniable. Cell enjoys teaching the lesson because he believes no one remains capable of improving on it.', 'A larger output is not automatically better performance. Optimize for the whole task, including speed, control, and endurance.', ['future_trunks', 'cell', 'vegeta'], ['grade_three', 'speed', 'failure']],
      ['A Different Super Saiyan Goal', 'Goku and Gohan enter the Hyperbolic Time Chamber after Vegeta and Trunks. Goku reaches the same power-heavy transformations but rejects their inefficiency. He instead trains with Gohan to make ordinary Super Saiyan form calm and natural, reducing its strain. Gohan’s hidden surges suggest that the student may contain the greater untapped power.', 'Goku studies the failed approach without contempt and chooses mastery over spectacle. Gohan learns beside a father who increasingly treats him as a capable partner.', 'The best advanced technique may be a stable foundation used without waste. Make excellence sustainable.', ['goku', 'gohan'], ['time_chamber', 'full_power_super_saiyan', 'training']],
      ['Ten Days Until the Games', 'Perfect Cell defeats Trunks but spares him, deciding that a public tournament will provide better opponents and entertainment. He constructs an arena, announces the Cell Games on television, and gives Earth ten days to prepare. Goku and Gohan emerge from the chamber before using their full allotted time, confident that rest and control now matter more than another exhausted year.', 'Cell turns global fear into a stage for validation. Goku’s calm unsettles his allies because they cannot yet see the judgment behind his confidence in Gohan.', 'More preparation is not always better preparation. Know when recovery will add more than another repetition.', ['cell', 'goku', 'gohan', 'future_trunks'], ['cell_games', 'deadline', 'training']],
      ['A Crisis Given a Date', 'Cell has reached perfection and chosen to pause the conflict for a tournament, while the defenders possess ten days and a clearer measure of his strength. This resolution ends before the Cell Games themselves. The immediate task is no longer pursuit or prevention, but deliberate preparation for a contest whose rules exist only as long as Cell enjoys them.', 'Goku trusts a path others cannot yet evaluate, Vegeta confronts the cost of his pride, and Trunks carries both greater strength and sharper humility into the deadline.', 'A deadline can turn panic into structure. Prepare for the stated challenge and the opponent who may abandon it.', ['cell', 'goku', 'gohan', 'vegeta', 'future_trunks'], ['resolution', 'cell_games', 'deadline']],
      ['Perfection Is Not Mastery', 'Cell’s completed form appears perfect because it combines selected strengths and fulfills his design. This final beat adds no event beyond the Games announcement. It reflects the arc’s contrast between acquisition and mastery: Cell absorbs power, Vegeta flaunts it, Trunks overbuilds it, while Goku and Gohan seek a state they can inhabit calmly.', 'Trunks grows most when he recognizes a flaw, not when his muscles expand. Goku’s approach suggests that controlled, sustainable power can surpass force assembled to impress.', 'Do not confuse completion with mastery. A finished design still has to work under real conditions.', ['cell', 'goku', 'gohan', 'vegeta', 'future_trunks'], ['mastery', 'perfection', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_cell_games: pack('dbz_cell_games', 'Cell Games Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: the fighters enter Cell’s tournament, Gohan reaches Super Saiyan 2, and Cell is destroyed.', [
      ['The World Comes to Cell', 'The defenders gather at Cell’s arena as the tournament is broadcast to a frightened world. Mr. Satan arrives with students and a public reputation built in ordinary martial arts, unaware of the scale before him. Cell dismisses the spectacle easily, while Goku steps forward as the first fighter who understands what the contest can actually demand.', 'Mr. Satan’s confidence depends on a world where tricks explain the impossible. Goku ignores the performance around him and studies Cell with clear respect for the danger.', 'A noisy room can obscure the real standard. Identify the challenge before measuring yourself against it.', ['cell', 'goku', 'mr_satan', 'gohan'], ['cell_games', 'tournament', 'broadcast']],
      ['Goku Tests the Champion', 'Goku and Cell trade high-speed attacks across the arena and sky, each revealing techniques familiar from earlier battles. Cell destroys the ring after deciding its boundary is inconvenient, abandoning the tournament’s formal loss condition. Goku fights intelligently and recovers from severe exchanges, but eventually concludes that continuing would not produce the victory Earth needs.', 'Goku enjoys the contest without forgetting its purpose. Cell treats rules as decoration and assumes Goku’s withdrawal proves that no deeper plan remains for long.', 'Testing limits is useful when you can interpret the result. Stop before persistence becomes denial.', ['goku', 'cell'], ['duel', 'cell_games', 'strategy']],
      ['The Choice No One Expected', 'Goku concedes and names Gohan as Cell’s next opponent, even giving Cell a senzu bean so the test will begin evenly. The others are horrified, and Gohan explains that he dislikes fighting despite the power his father has sensed. Cell attacks to force that buried strength outward, while Gohan struggles to reconcile capacity with reluctance.', 'Goku trusts Gohan’s potential but misjudges how differently his son experiences combat. Gohan’s aversion is not cowardice; he fears what anger may make him become.', 'Knowing someone’s capability is not the same as understanding their consent or motivation. Ask before relying on both.', ['goku', 'gohan', 'cell'], ['gohan', 'senzu', 'expectations']],
      ['Sixteen’s Last Appeal', 'Cell creates Cell Juniors and sends them against Goku’s injured allies, hoping their suffering will provoke Gohan. Android 16 attempts to destroy Cell with a removed explosive device, but Bulma had taken it out during repairs. His damaged head asks Gohan to release the anger used for protection. Cell crushes him, and Gohan’s restraint finally breaks.', 'Sixteen, built as a weapon, values living things and gives Gohan permission to stop confusing gentleness with passivity. Gohan’s grief focuses on preventable cruelty rather than wounded pride.', 'Kindness needs boundaries strong enough to defend life. Refusing needless harm may require decisive force.', ['android_16', 'gohan', 'cell', 'cell_juniors'], ['android_16', 'cell_juniors', 'anger']],
      ['Gohan Ascends', 'Gohan transforms into Super Saiyan 2 and destroys the Cell Juniors with effortless speed before dominating Cell. His attacks force Cell to expel Android 18 and revert to a less complete form. Yet Gohan prolongs the punishment rather than finish immediately, allowing new confidence and anger to create the opening Cell needs for a desperate response.', 'Gohan finally accepts his power, then begins savoring Cell’s fear. Goku recognizes that the breakthrough he anticipated carries the exact danger Gohan had feared now.', 'A justified advantage can still distort judgment. Complete the protective task before satisfaction rewrites the goal.', ['gohan', 'cell', 'android_18', 'cell_juniors'], ['super_saiyan_2', 'pride', 'turning_point']],
      ['Goku’s Instant Farewell', 'Cell prepares to self-destruct and take Earth with him after losing his perfect form. Gohan realizes too late that he could have ended the fight sooner. Goku uses Instant Transmission to carry Cell to King Kai’s planet, where the explosion kills Goku, King Kai, and Bubbles while sparing Earth. The apparent victory lasts only moments.', 'Goku corrects the crisis through immediate sacrifice without condemning Gohan. Gohan must face the consequences of delay without allowing guilt to end his ability to act.', 'When a mistake creates an emergency, accountability begins with the next useful action, not self-punishment.', ['goku', 'gohan', 'cell', 'king_kai'], ['sacrifice', 'instant_transmission', 'self_destruction']],
      ['The Beam from Father and Son', 'Cell regenerates from a surviving core, returns in perfect form, and kills Trunks. Vegeta attacks recklessly in grief; Gohan shields him and injures an arm. With Goku encouraging him from the Other World, Gohan meets Cell’s final Kamehameha. Vegeta’s distraction creates an opening, and Gohan releases enough power to erase Cell completely.', 'Gohan fights through injury and guilt by accepting support he cannot physically see. Vegeta’s grief breaks his detachment, and one imperfect intervention helps decide the struggle.', 'You do not have to feel whole to finish necessary work. Use the support and opening available.', ['gohan', 'goku', 'cell', 'vegeta', 'future_trunks'], ['father_son_kamehameha', 'cell_defeat', 'teamwork']],
      ['The Cost After Victory', 'The Dragon Balls restore Cell’s victims, though Goku chooses to remain dead, believing his presence has repeatedly attracted danger. Android 18 survives, and Krillin uses the available wish to remove the explosives from both her and Seventeen. Trunks returns to his future with the strength and knowledge to defeat its androids and Cell.', 'Gohan returns to family carrying victory and loss. Krillin’s wish respects Eighteen without trying to control her, while Trunks converts the past timeline’s help into liberation at home.', 'Resolution is more than reversing damage. Preserve autonomy, honor loss, and carry useful change forward.', ['gohan', 'goku', 'krillin', 'android_18', 'future_trunks'], ['aftermath', 'dragon_balls', 'future']],
      ['The Gentle Fighter’s Strength', 'The Cell Games end with Earth safe and Gohan established as its decisive defender, but the result was never a solitary triumph. This mastery entry adds no canon event. It reflects a chain of training, warnings, errors, sacrifices, interventions, and trust that allowed a reluctant fighter to use anger without surrendering his deeper gentleness.', 'Gohan’s power matters because he ultimately directs it toward protection. Goku’s confidence was partly right and partly incomplete, a reminder that faith in someone must include listening to them.', 'Integrate strength with temperament. The goal is not becoming harder, but becoming able to protect what softness values.', ['gohan', 'goku', 'cell', 'android_16'], ['mastery', 'gohan', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_other_world: pack('dbz_other_world', 'Other World Saga', 'anime_only', 'Anime-only Dragon Ball Z continuation: Goku meets Pikkon and competes in the Other World Tournament after Cell’s defeat.', [
      ['A Hero Among the Dead', 'After choosing to remain in the Other World, Goku travels with King Kai and encounters warriors trained by the other directional Kais. When trouble breaks out in Hell, Goku meets West Kai’s student Pikkon, whose disciplined power makes him an immediate peer. Their success leads toward a tournament honoring the strongest deceased fighters.', 'Goku treats death as another horizon for learning, while Pikkon carries himself with reserved focus. King Kai’s rivalry with West Kai adds comic pride around serious talent.', 'A changed circumstance can still contain meaningful work. Look for the next arena of growth.', ['goku', 'pikkon', 'king_kai', 'west_kai'], ['anime_only', 'other_world', 'pikkon']],
      ['The Other World Tournament', 'Grand Kai permits a tournament among fighters from across the Other World. Goku advances through unfamiliar opponents with techniques and histories outside Earth’s martial arts. Pikkon progresses from the other side of the bracket, establishing himself as the likely final test. The competition broadens Goku’s understanding of strength beyond the rivals he knew in life.', 'Goku meets novelty with delighted attention rather than defensiveness. Pikkon values precision and composure, making him a contrast to Goku’s open enthusiasm through every exchange.', 'New peers reveal dimensions that familiar competition cannot. Enter the wider field ready to learn.', ['goku', 'pikkon', 'grand_kai'], ['anime_only', 'tournament', 'other_world']],
      ['Two Champions Meet', 'Goku and Pikkon reach the final and exchange techniques powerful enough to threaten the tournament grounds. Pikkon’s Thunder Flash forces Goku to study its rhythm instead of simply enduring it. Goku finds a narrow counter through Instant Transmission, and both fighters push beyond what their earlier matches required, turning the final into mutual discovery.', 'Pikkon’s disciplined attack is formidable but repeatable enough to read. Goku’s improvisation succeeds because he studies while fighting rather than waiting for certainty under pressure.', 'Patterns create openings. Pay attention inside pressure, especially when the obvious response has failed; then move decisively.', ['goku', 'pikkon'], ['anime_only', 'final', 'instant_transmission']],
      ['A Technical Disqualification', 'The final ends without a formal champion when Grand Kai rules that both Goku and Pikkon touched the arena ceiling, violating the boundary. Grand Kai postpones the promised lesson for the winner by an absurdly long span. The decision does not erase their performance: each has gained a rival and a clearer view of what further training might demand.', 'Goku accepts the anticlimax with good humor, and Pikkon retains dignity without needing a trophy to validate the contest. Grand Kai quietly avoids a promise he was not ready to fulfill.', 'A technical result can differ from the value of the work. Keep the growth even when the prize disappears.', ['goku', 'pikkon', 'grand_kai'], ['anime_only', 'disqualification', 'rivalry']],
      ['Training Beyond an Ending', 'This anime-only tournament leaves Goku in the Other World with new peers and no official victory. The final beat adds no further occurrence and does not extend the manga’s plot. It reflects the idea that competition can remain valuable without permanent stakes, a trophy, or a clean conclusion when it supplies respect and a sharper path forward.', 'Goku and Pikkon finish as rivals who have expanded one another’s standards. Neither needs the other diminished for the contest to have mattered without resentment.', 'Let worthy competition enlarge your craft. A disputed finish does not cancel an honest test.', ['goku', 'pikkon'], ['mastery', 'anime_only', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_great_saiyaman: pack('dbz_great_saiyaman', 'Great Saiyaman Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: seven years after Cell, teenage Gohan enters school, adopts a superhero identity, and meets Videl.', [
      ['A Scholar in Satan City', 'Seven years after Cell’s defeat, Gohan begins attending Orange Star High School in Satan City. He has grown into a powerful but sheltered teenager focused on his studies. Stopping criminals on the way to class makes classmates wonder about the mysterious fighter, and Videl, Mr. Satan’s daughter, starts examining the new student’s convenient appearances.', 'Gohan can defeat criminals easily but finds ordinary attention much harder to manage. Videl observes details others dismiss and refuses to let celebrity substitute for evidence.', 'Competence in one setting does not guarantee ease in another. Learn the social terrain too.', ['gohan', 'videl', 'mr_satan'], ['school', 'seven_years', 'identity']],
      ['The Great Saiyaman Appears', 'Gohan asks Bulma for a disguise that will let him help people without exposing his identity. She creates a transformation watch and costume, and Gohan invents the Great Saiyaman persona with dramatic poses. The disguise hides his face more effectively than his habits, especially as he keeps appearing whenever Videl encounters trouble around the city.', 'Gohan enjoys the performance more than his embarrassed audience does. Bulma solves the technical problem, but Videl understands that mannerisms can reveal what clothing conceals.', 'A mask protects only the information it actually changes. Habits often identify us more reliably than appearance.', ['gohan', 'bulma', 'videl'], ['great_saiyaman', 'disguise', 'school']],
      ['Videl Solves the Mystery', 'Videl connects Gohan’s reactions, absences, and unusual athletic ability to the Great Saiyaman. She confronts him and secures his participation in the upcoming World Martial Arts Tournament in exchange for keeping the secret. When she learns he can fly, she also insists that he teach her, turning suspicion into an unusual training partnership.', 'Videl wins leverage through observation rather than force. Gohan is flustered by exposure, yet he agrees to teach instead of treating his knowledge as private property.', 'Being discovered can become collaboration. Set fair terms and use the new honesty constructively together.', ['gohan', 'videl'], ['identity_reveal', 'world_tournament', 'flight']],
      ['Learning to Fly', 'Gohan teaches Videl how to sense and control her energy, and he includes Goten when his younger brother asks to learn. Videl cuts her hair for practicality and steadily achieves flight through patience. News of the tournament brings the wider group together, including Goku, who receives permission to return from the Other World for one day.', 'Gohan proves a patient teacher when he translates instinct into steps. Videl’s progress comes from concentration and repetition, while Goten’s natural talent surprises his brother.', 'Teaching reveals what intuition hides. Explain the foundation, then give practice room to work deliberately.', ['gohan', 'videl', 'goten', 'goku'], ['flight_training', 'teaching', 'reunion']],
      ['A Double Life Integrated', 'Gohan’s school life, rescue work, exposed disguise, and training sessions lead him toward the World Martial Arts Tournament with friends and family. This mastery entry adds no later tournament event. It reflects a young hero learning that ordinary relationships need honesty and patience as much as spectacular crises need strength.', 'Gohan does not have to choose permanently between scholar, son, teacher, and protector. Videl challenges secrecy but also proves capable of meeting the truth with effort.', 'Maturity is often integration rather than reinvention. Let each role inform the others without letting one consume them.', ['gohan', 'videl', 'goten'], ['mastery', 'identity', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_world_tournament: pack('dbz_world_tournament', 'World Tournament Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Goku returns for one day, the heroes enter the tournament, and Spopovich steals Gohan’s energy.', [
      ['One Day Together', 'Goku returns to Earth for a single day and reunites with family and friends at the World Martial Arts Tournament. He meets seven-year-old Goten, whose resemblance makes the missed years immediately visible. Vegeta, Gohan, Krillin, Piccolo, and Android 18 also enter, giving the gathering the warmth of a reunion and the tension of serious competition.', 'Goku welcomes Goten with uncomplicated affection, while Gohan watches a family reconnect under a deadline. Vegeta sees the tournament as his long-awaited chance to face Goku again.', 'Limited time makes priorities visible. Be fully present before trying to make the day impressive.', ['goku', 'goten', 'gohan', 'vegeta', 'krillin', 'android_18'], ['reunion', 'tournament', 'family']],
      ['The Junior Final', 'Goten and Trunks dominate the junior division despite agreeing not to transform. They meet in the final, where Trunks wins after both children test the limits of their rules. Frustrated that they cannot enter the adult division normally, they later disguise themselves as the masked fighter Mighty Mask, combining their small bodies inside one costume.', 'Goten and Trunks turn friendship into delighted rivalry, but their shortcut toward adult competition is unstable by design. Trunks’s victory matters less to them than the shared challenge.', 'Playful competition can build skill. Keep the rules clear enough that cleverness does not become confusion.', ['goten', 'kid_trunks'], ['junior_division', 'rivalry', 'mighty_mask']],
      ['Unfamiliar Entrants', 'The adult drawing produces strange matchups, including Piccolo against the quiet Shin and Gohan against Kibito. Piccolo withdraws after sensing that Shin’s identity and authority exceed an ordinary fighter. The group also notices Spopovich and Yamu, men whose disturbing energy and unnatural endurance suggest that the tournament has attracted a threat unrelated to its prize.', 'Piccolo respects intuition strong enough to override public pride. Shin watches the fighters carefully because he needs their power against a danger they have not yet seen.', 'Withdrawal can be intelligent when new information changes the purpose of the contest. Curiosity should follow.', ['piccolo', 'shin', 'kibito', 'spopovich', 'yamu'], ['supreme_kai', 'tournament', 'mystery']],
      ['Videl Will Not Stay Down', 'Videl faces Spopovich and initially outclasses him, but he survives injuries that should end the match and attacks her with prolonged cruelty. Gohan struggles not to intervene as she repeatedly rises. Videl is finally defeated and rushed for treatment, while Gohan’s anger exposes how far the tournament has moved from the honorable contest he expected.', 'Videl’s resolve is genuine, but Spopovich’s magically reinforced body turns courage into exposure. Gohan must respect her agency while watching rules fail to protect her.', 'Perseverance is not an obligation to absorb limitless harm. Systems need safeguards, not admiration for suffering.', ['videl', 'spopovich', 'gohan'], ['videl', 'spopovich', 'tournament']],
      ['Gohan’s Power Revealed', 'Kibito asks Gohan to transform, and Gohan displays his Super Saiyan 2 power before the arena. Shin restrains him psychically while Spopovich and Yamu use a device to drain his energy, then flee. The apparent betrayal is part of Shin’s attempt to locate their master, but the plan leaves Gohan collapsed and the others furious.', 'Gohan cooperates with Kibito without knowing the full stakes. Shin accepts causing immediate harm because he believes following the stolen energy is the only route to a planetary threat.', 'Need-to-know plans carry moral cost when allies bear the risk. Share enough context to preserve informed trust.', ['gohan', 'kibito', 'shin', 'spopovich', 'yamu'], ['energy_theft', 'super_saiyan_2', 'babidi']],
      ['The Tournament Is Left Behind', 'Kibito restores Gohan’s energy, and Shin explains that the theft will lead them to the wizard Babidi, who is gathering power to revive Majin Buu. Goku, Vegeta, Gohan, Piccolo, and Krillin abandon the tournament to follow. Android 18 remains, eventually maneuvering the final match so Mr. Satan keeps his reputation in exchange for payment.', 'The fighters leave reunion and rivalry behind when the stakes become clear. Eighteen treats the remaining spectacle as a practical negotiation rather than a sacred contest.', 'When the real objective appears, release the attractive but smaller one. Attention is a strategic resource.', ['shin', 'goku', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'piccolo', 'krillin', 'android_18'], ['resolution', 'babidi', 'pursuit']],
      ['The Day Changes Direction', 'The tournament begins as a reunion and competition but ends with most of Earth’s defenders pursuing stolen energy toward an unknown wizard. This final beat adds no event from Babidi’s ship. It reflects how quickly celebration can reveal new duties, and how character appears in the willingness to leave a desired contest unfinished.', 'Goku and Vegeta surrender their anticipated rematch for the immediate pursuit, though the rivalry remains unresolved. Gohan follows the trail created through his own stolen strength.', 'Plans deserve commitment, not worship. Change direction when stronger evidence changes what matters most now.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'shin'], ['mastery', 'priorities', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_babidi: pack('dbz_babidi', 'Babidi Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: the heroes invade Babidi’s ship, Vegeta accepts the Majin mark, and the energy from his duel awakens Buu.', [
      ['The Ship Beneath the Wasteland', 'Shin leads Goku, Vegeta, Gohan, Piccolo, and Krillin to Babidi’s buried ship. They watch Dabura kill Kibito and turn Piccolo and Krillin to stone with his spit. Shin explains that killing Dabura can reverse the petrification. Goku, Vegeta, and Gohan follow the wizard inside, where staged battles will feed their damage into Buu’s sealed energy.', 'Shin carries ancient fear of Buu but little confidence in the Saiyans’ informal approach. Vegeta resents being treated as fuel and believes no servant on the ship can challenge him.', 'Understanding an enemy’s resource model changes every exchange. Do not keep paying their costs without calculation.', ['shin', 'goku', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'babidi', 'dabura', 'piccolo', 'krillin'], ['babidi_ship', 'petrification', 'majin_buu']],
      ['Two Floors, Two Reversals', 'Babidi sends Vegeta to a world with gravity ten times Earth’s, but Vegeta’s training makes Pui Pui’s advantage ordinary and he destroys the servant. On the next floor, Yakon consumes light energy in darkness suited to his senses. Goku deliberately offers increasing Super Saiyan power until Yakon takes in more than he can contain and explodes.', 'Vegeta neutralizes the environment through preparation. Goku turns an absorption ability against its owner, while Shin realizes that Babidi’s defenses were built on badly outdated assumptions.', 'Preparation and observation can reverse designed advantages. Find whether the limit belongs to the environment, the user, or both.', ['vegeta', 'pui_pui', 'goku', 'yakon', 'shin', 'babidi'], ['babidi_ship', 'gravity', 'energy_absorption']],
      ['Dabura Reads the Rivalry', 'Gohan fights Dabura but lacks the sharpness he displayed against Cell, frustrating Vegeta. Dabura withdraws after sensing the darkness in Vegeta’s heart and tells Babidi that a stronger source of conflict is available. The wizard exploits Vegeta’s resentment and places the Majin mark on him, drawing out power while trying to claim obedience.', 'Gohan’s neglected training has consequences under real pressure. Vegeta permits the corruption because he wants access to the ruthless focus he associates with his former self.', 'A shortcut that amplifies strength may also target an unresolved wound. Examine what it asks to control.', ['gohan', 'dabura', 'vegeta', 'babidi'], ['dabura', 'majin_vegeta', 'temptation']],
      ['The Price of a Rematch', 'Babidi transports the group back to the tournament grounds, where Majin Vegeta kills spectators to force Goku into their postponed fight. Goku agrees only after Vegeta threatens further deaths, and they move to an isolated area. Their Super Saiyan 2 battle releases exactly the energy Babidi needs, even though Vegeta resists the wizard’s direct commands.', 'Vegeta proves his will is not Babidi’s, yet freely chooses actions shaped by obsession. Goku sees that refusing the duel will not undo the danger Vegeta has created.', 'Freedom from control does not excuse a destructive choice. Agency increases responsibility rather than reducing it.', ['majin_vegeta', 'goku', 'babidi'], ['majin_vegeta', 'rivalry', 'energy']],
      ['Buu Wakes', 'Gohan and Shin reach the sealed chamber but cannot stop the energy meter from filling. Majin Buu emerges as a round, childlike creature whose playful manner does not match Shin’s terror. Dabura attacks after judging Buu uncontrollable; Buu turns him into food, restoring Piccolo and Krillin from stone. Babidi quickly uses the threat of resealing to establish leverage.', 'Shin recognizes the ancient destroyer beneath Buu’s appearance. Babidi mistakes temporary leverage for true authority over a being whose impulses he barely understands at all.', 'Do not confuse a harmless manner with harmless capacity. Assess behavior, power, and incentives separately.', ['majin_buu', 'gohan', 'shin', 'dabura', 'babidi'], ['majin_buu', 'awakening', 'dabura']],
      ['The Rivalry Meets Its Consequence', 'Majin Buu is awake, Dabura is gone, and the stolen energy has transformed a personal duel into a planetary emergency. Goku and Vegeta sense the new power and stop their fight, but the damage enabling the awakening cannot be recalled. This resolution ends before Vegeta confronts Buu and before the creature begins its wider rampage.', 'Vegeta finally sees that his desired rematch served Babidi’s design. Goku turns from rivalry toward the threat, carrying the cost of agreeing to the battle.', 'When consequences outgrow the original dispute, end the dispute immediately. Repair begins with shared reality.', ['majin_buu', 'goku', 'majin_vegeta', 'babidi', 'shin'], ['resolution', 'awakening', 'consequences']],
      ['Manipulation Needs an Opening', 'Babidi succeeds not by overpowering every defender, but by arranging fights that harvest energy and exploiting Vegeta’s unresolved need to surpass Goku. This mastery entry adds no new event after Buu’s awakening. It reflects how personal wounds can become strategic vulnerabilities, even when the person involved remains strong enough to defy direct control.', 'Vegeta resists Babidi’s commands but not his own obsession, which makes the distinction between independence and self-mastery painfully clear. Gohan’s lost edge also shows that old success cannot replace current practice.', 'Guard the motive an adversary would recruit. Self-knowledge closes doors that raw willpower leaves open.', ['babidi', 'majin_vegeta', 'goku', 'gohan'], ['mastery', 'manipulation', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_buu: pack('dbz_buu', 'Majin Buu Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Fat Buu devastates Earth, Vegeta sacrifices himself, Goku reveals Super Saiyan 3, and Buu splits into good and evil halves.', [
      ['Vegeta’s Final Explosion', 'Vegeta knocks Goku unconscious and confronts Majin Buu alone after the creature overwhelms Gohan and Shin. He embraces Trunks for the first time, sends both children away with Piccolo, and releases all his energy in a self-destructive blast meant to erase Buu. Vegeta dies, but fragments of Buu survive and reassemble after the battlefield falls quiet.', 'Vegeta’s sacrifice is an honest act of protection after choices that helped cause the crisis. Piccolo cannot promise him a peaceful afterlife, yet Vegeta proceeds without bargaining for absolution.', 'Repair may demand sacrifice, but one noble act does not erase earlier harm. It can still begin change.', ['vegeta', 'majin_buu', 'kid_trunks', 'piccolo'], ['sacrifice', 'final_explosion', 'majin_buu']],
      ['A Dance and a Third Form', 'With Vegeta dead and Gohan believed lost, Goku teaches Goten and Trunks the Fusion Dance so they can become Earth’s next defender. He then confronts Buu and Babidi to buy time for Trunks to retrieve the Dragon Radar. Goku reveals Super Saiyan 3, whose enormous power shakes Earth but rapidly consumes his remaining borrowed time, and withdraws once the mission succeeds.', 'Goku transfers knowledge before using spectacle as a diversion. The form’s cost prevents a long rescue, while Buu responds to its power with curiosity rather than loyalty to Babidi.', 'A powerful tool can buy time for a handoff. Match its duration and cost to the actual mission.', ['goku', 'goten', 'kid_trunks', 'majin_buu', 'babidi'], ['fusion_dance', 'super_saiyan_3', 'delay']],
      ['Buu Rejects His Master', 'Babidi repeatedly insults and threatens Buu, relying on the possibility of resealing him. Goku points out that Buu is strong enough to refuse. After Goku leaves, Buu turns on Babidi and kills him, removing the only person who knew the sealing phrase. Free from commands, Buu continues destructive play because freedom has not given him a moral compass.', 'Buu recognizes abuse and ends it, but he has no learned boundary between liberation and cruelty. Babidi’s control fails because humiliation eventually outweighs fear alone.', 'Escaping a harmful authority is essential; learning what should guide you afterward is a separate task.', ['majin_buu', 'babidi', 'goku'], ['babidi_death', 'freedom', 'majin_buu']],
      ['Mr. Satan Finds the Person', 'Mr. Satan approaches Buu intending to use tricks, but gradually befriends him instead. He explains that killing is wrong, and Buu agrees to stop after discovering companionship and caring for an injured dog named Bee. The unlikely household reveals that Buu can learn empathy through relationship more effectively than through threats or attacks.', 'Mr. Satan begins from fear and self-interest but stays long enough to act with genuine care. Buu responds because he is addressed as a person capable of choosing.', 'Some dangerous behavior changes through connection when punishment has failed. Keep judgment, but test for teachability.', ['mr_satan', 'majin_buu', 'bee'], ['friendship', 'bee', 'change']],
      ['Good and Evil Divide', 'Gunmen wound Bee and nearly kill Mr. Satan, provoking Buu’s rage. He heals his friends but expels the evil within himself as a thin gray counterpart. The evil Buu overpowers the good half, turns him into chocolate, and consumes him. The resulting Super Buu retains immense power with far less restraint and immediately becomes a new global threat.', 'Good Buu tries to preserve the values he learned, but accumulated violence takes separate form. Mr. Satan’s friendship remains real even though it cannot contain the transformation.', 'Progress can be fragile under trauma. Protect the supports around change, and prepare for relapse without denying growth.', ['majin_buu', 'evil_buu', 'super_buu', 'mr_satan', 'bee'], ['buu_split', 'super_buu', 'trauma']],
      ['A Different Buu Emerges', 'Fat Buu’s rampage has ended in a split: his gentler portion is absorbed, and Super Buu now carries the advantage. Goku has returned to the Other World, Gohan is training elsewhere under the Kais, and the children continue preparing fusion. This resolution stops before Super Buu reaches the Lookout or battles any fused warrior.', 'Buu demonstrates that moral development was possible but not yet stable. Mr. Satan’s influence survives as evidence that the good half existed, even inside a worse outcome.', 'When a problem changes form, preserve what you learned from the earlier version and reassess every capability.', ['super_buu', 'majin_buu', 'mr_satan', 'goku', 'gohan'], ['resolution', 'super_buu', 'transition']],
      ['Power Can Learn, and Unlearn', 'The first Buu conflict moves from magical control through sacrifice and training to an unexpected experiment in friendship, then fractures into a more dangerous form. This mastery beat adds no event after Super Buu emerges. It reflects the unsettling truth that a destructive being showed real capacity for change, though the conditions supporting it proved vulnerable.', 'Vegeta acts selflessly without surviving to see the result. Mr. Satan achieves what force did not by teaching Buu a boundary, and that achievement still matters after the split.', 'Take signs of change seriously without assuming they are permanent. Reinforcement is part of transformation.', ['majin_buu', 'vegeta', 'mr_satan', 'super_buu'], ['mastery', 'change', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_fusion: pack('dbz_fusion', 'Fusion Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Gotenks and Ultimate Gohan battle Super Buu, who absorbs them before Vegito engineers a rescue.', [
      ['Super Buu Finds the Lookout', 'Super Buu reaches Kami’s Lookout and demands the promised challenger. To buy the children time, Piccolo directs him to eliminate Earth’s remaining population, which Buu does from the Lookout with a sweeping attack. Piccolo then leads him slowly toward the Hyperbolic Time Chamber while Goten and Trunks complete their final preparations inside.', 'Piccolo manages an impossible delay with composure, but every gained minute carries a terrible cost. Super Buu shows more focus than his earlier form and far less openness to influence.', 'Buying time is not automatically a victory. Account honestly for who pays for every delay.', ['super_buu', 'piccolo', 'goten', 'kid_trunks'], ['lookout', 'human_extinction_attack', 'time_chamber']],
      ['Gotenks Takes the Stage', 'Goten and Trunks fuse into Gotenks and fight Super Buu inside the chamber. After Gotenks pretends to be out of options, Piccolo destroys the entrance to trap Buu. Buu screams open a dimensional escape and returns to the Lookout. Only then does Gotenks reveal Super Saiyan 3, create a similar breach, and follow him out.', 'Gotenks possesses spectacular power but wastes time performing and hiding his best form. Piccolo’s containment plan fails because neither he nor Buu understood the limits of rage.', 'Do not save the effective tool for dramatic timing when the real deadline is already closing.', ['gotenks', 'super_buu', 'piccolo'], ['fusion', 'super_saiyan_3', 'time_chamber']],
      ['The Fusion Runs Out', 'On the Lookout, Gotenks battles Super Buu as a Super Saiyan 3 and appears capable of winning. Before he can finish, the thirty-minute fusion expires, separating him into Goten and Trunks. Gohan then returns from the Sacred World of the Kai with his potential fully awakened and takes control of the battle without transforming into a Super Saiyan.', 'Gotenks learns that enormous output cannot ignore a hard time limit. Gohan arrives with quiet strength developed through ritual and patience rather than visible transformation.', 'Time-limited power needs a finish condition. Track the clock as carefully as you track the opponent.', ['gotenks', 'super_buu', 'gohan', 'goten', 'kid_trunks'], ['fusion_limit', 'ultimate_gohan', 'lookout']],
      ['Buu Turns Strength into Bait', 'Unable to match Gohan directly, Super Buu triggers a calculated self-destruction and returns after the boys can fuse again. He absorbs Gotenks and Piccolo, gaining their power and Piccolo’s tactical intelligence. The advantage shifts immediately, and Gohan is forced from confident control into a battle against the combined strengths of his own allies.', 'Buu adapts by making the defenders’ strongest asset his target. Gohan is powerful but slow to recognize that the apparent rematch was designed around absorption.', 'When an opponent cannot beat your advantage, expect them to capture, bypass, or redefine it.', ['super_buu', 'gohan', 'gotenks', 'piccolo'], ['absorption', 'buutenks', 'strategy']],
      ['Vegito Refuses the Obvious Finish', 'Goku returns to Earth with Potara earrings and fuses with Vegeta after Buu absorbs Gohan. Vegito overwhelms the resulting form, resisting even an attempt to turn him into candy. Rather than destroy Buu immediately, Vegito deliberately allows himself to be absorbed behind a protective barrier, intending to rescue the people trapped inside.', 'Goku and Vegeta achieve extraordinary coordination despite their rivalry. Vegito’s mockery conceals a rescue plan that values the absorbed victims over the simplest victory inside Buu.', 'The fastest finish is not always the complete solution. Define victory to include the people still inside the problem.', ['vegito', 'super_buu', 'goku', 'vegeta', 'gohan'], ['potara', 'vegito', 'rescue']],
      ['The Absorbed Are Free', 'Vegito separates inside Buu, returning Goku and Vegeta to individual bodies. They free Gohan, Piccolo, Goten, and Trunks from organic pods and escape with the rescued fighters as Buu convulses outside. Vegeta also removes Fat Buu’s pod, undoing the absorbed influences that shaped Super Buu. This resolution stops before the resulting pure form destroys Earth.', 'Vegeta refuses permanent fusion yet works beside Goku through the rescue. Their success restores allies as people rather than components, though removing Fat Buu carries an unknown consequence.', 'A rescue can alter the whole system. Restore people, then prepare for what removing each component may release.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'gohan', 'piccolo', 'goten', 'kid_trunks', 'majin_buu', 'super_buu'], ['resolution', 'inside_buu', 'rescue']],
      ['Combination and Identity', 'Fusion repeatedly changes what one fighter can do: Gotenks multiplies youthful power, Buu steals identities as resources, and Vegito joins two rivals by consent to stage a rescue. This mastery entry adds no event after the captives are freed. It reflects how combination can express cooperation or violation depending on agency, purpose, and what happens to the people involved.', 'Goku and Vegeta accept union only when separate strength cannot reach the captives. Buu pursues combination as consumption, while the rescued fighters regain identities he treated as equipment.', 'Shared power is strongest when consent and purpose survive the joining. Never confuse unity with erasure.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'vegito', 'super_buu', 'gotenks'], ['mastery', 'fusion', 'reflection']],
    ]),

    dbz_kid_buu: pack('dbz_kid_buu', 'Kid Buu Saga', 'canon_core', 'Core Dragon Ball Z story: Kid Buu destroys Earth, battles on the Kai world, and falls to a Spirit Bomb powered by Earth’s people.', [
      ['The Pure Form Destroys Earth', 'After the absorptions are removed, Buu contracts into Kid Buu, a smaller form driven by destruction without Super Buu’s calculation. He immediately forms an attack capable of erasing Earth. Goku and Vegeta escape to the Sacred World of the Kai with Dende, Mr. Satan, and Bee, but they cannot reach Gohan, Piccolo, Goten, or Trunks before the planet explodes.', 'Goku chooses the nearest people in a fraction of a second and is devastated by those left behind. Kid Buu offers no demand to negotiate because destruction is the action itself.', 'Some emergencies permit no complete rescue. Make the best reachable choice, then face the loss without falsifying it.', ['kid_buu', 'goku', 'vegeta', 'mr_satan', 'bee', 'dende'], ['earth_destroyed', 'kid_buu', 'escape']],
      ['A Trail of Vanished Worlds', 'Kid Buu reforms after Earth’s destruction and searches for Goku and Vegeta. On the Sacred World of the Kai, they deliberately raise their energy to draw him away from surviving populations. Buu follows the signal to their remote battlefield, concentrating the final confrontation where another inhabited world will not pay for it.', 'Goku and Vegeta turn themselves into a signal because directing danger is now part of defending everyone else. Kid Buu follows impulse with frightening speed.', 'Containment begins with choosing where the crisis unfolds. Move the risk away from those who cannot consent to it.', ['kid_buu', 'goku', 'vegeta', 'shin'], ['sacred_world', 'pursuit', 'battlefield']],
      ['Goku’s Minute of Full Power', 'Goku fights Kid Buu as a Super Saiyan 3 and appears capable of matching him, but the living body cannot sustain the form as easily as Goku’s dead body did. Vegeta takes over so Goku can gather power for one minute. Kid Buu repeatedly crushes Vegeta, who continues rising despite knowing he is buying time rather than winning.', 'Goku discovers that a familiar transformation now carries different physical rules. Vegeta finally acknowledges Goku’s greatness while contributing through endurance instead of rivalry at last.', 'A changed context can change the cost of a proven tool. Recalculate before relying on old performance.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'kid_buu'], ['super_saiyan_3', 'delay', 'respect']],
      ['Good Buu and Mr. Satan Intervene', 'Fat Buu emerges from Kid Buu and joins the fight, giving Vegeta another defender to rotate into the battle. Mr. Satan survives through luck and unexpected goodwill, then pulls the injured Vegeta clear when Goku cannot attack safely. Kid Buu expels the good Buu from his body entirely and continues fighting both halves of his own history.', 'Good Buu protects the friend who taught him restraint. Mr. Satan, physically weakest on the field, saves Vegeta at the exact moment strength cannot solve positioning.', 'Contribution is contextual. The least powerful person may still be the only one placed to act.', ['majin_buu', 'mr_satan', 'vegeta', 'goku', 'kid_buu'], ['good_buu', 'mr_satan', 'rescue']],
      ['Vegeta’s Plan Uses the Dragon Balls', 'Vegeta rejects another private duel and proposes a Spirit Bomb powered by Earth’s people. Porunga restores Earth, revives everyone killed since the tournament except the most evil, and transports Dende away from danger. Goku begins gathering willing energy, but most people distrust the unseen request and contribute too little while Kid Buu keeps pressing the battle.', 'Vegeta designs a victory that depends on the population he once attacked. Goku can ask for energy, but reputation and distance limit the immediate response.', 'A collective plan needs trusted communication as much as sound mechanics. Build credibility before the emergency.', ['vegeta', 'goku', 'porunga', 'dende', 'kid_buu'], ['dragon_balls', 'earth_restored', 'spirit_bomb']],
      ['The World Listens to Its Champion', 'Vegeta appeals to Earth, but the population largely ignores a voice they do not know. Mr. Satan speaks instead, and people recognize the champion they trust. They raise their hands, supplying the vast energy needed for the Spirit Bomb. His public myth, often played for comedy, becomes the communication bridge that the true fighters lack.', 'Mr. Satan uses fame in service of others rather than himself. Vegeta accepts that the plan needs a human connection his power and pride cannot manufacture.', 'Trust is infrastructure. Expertise may design the solution, but a credible messenger helps people join it.', ['mr_satan', 'vegeta', 'goku', 'earthlings'], ['spirit_bomb', 'trust', 'collective_action']],
      ['The Final Spirit Bomb', 'Goku launches the completed Spirit Bomb, but exhaustion prevents him from forcing it past Kid Buu’s resistance. Dende uses the final Namekian wish to restore Goku’s energy. Returning to full strength, Goku becomes a Super Saiyan and drives the gathered power forward, destroying Kid Buu after wishing privately that the enemy might return someday as a good person.', 'Goku wins with energy freely given by others and recovery supplied through a wish, not by solitary power. Even at the finish, he imagines transformation beyond annihilation.', 'Accept the support that completes the task. Collective strength remains collective even when one person guides it.', ['goku', 'kid_buu', 'dende', 'porunga'], ['spirit_bomb', 'kid_buu_defeat', 'wish']],
      ['Peace and a New Opponent', 'Earth is restored, families reunite, and the good Buu lives peacefully under Mr. Satan’s protection, with public memories adjusted to allow his place in society. Ten years later, Goku enters the World Martial Arts Tournament to meet Uub, a kind village boy who is Kid Buu’s human reincarnation, and leaves to train him after recognizing his potential.', 'Mr. Satan turns friendship into lasting protection for Buu. Goku meets Uub without treating him as guilty for a former life, seeing a student and future defender instead.', 'A good future is more than restored normality. Invest in people who can carry strength differently.', ['goku', 'uub', 'majin_buu', 'mr_satan'], ['epilogue', 'uub', 'reincarnation']],
      ['A Victory Shared by Earth', 'Kid Buu’s defeat closes the long crisis through restored worlds, revived lives, Namekian wishes, good Buu’s resistance, Vegeta’s plan, Mr. Satan’s credibility, Earth’s energy, and Goku’s final guidance. This mastery beat adds no event beyond the ten-year reunion. It reflects a victory whose scale makes the myth of the solitary savior especially inadequate.', 'Vegeta stops treating combat as proof of rank and builds a collective answer. Goku delivers it, Mr. Satan makes it possible, and Uub embodies hope that destructive potential can return with a different nature.', 'Mastery includes knowing when the answer must belong to everyone. Lead the force you could never create alone.', ['goku', 'vegeta', 'mr_satan', 'majin_buu', 'uub'], ['mastery', 'collective_victory', 'reflection']],
    ]),
  });
})();
